- Framework: Flutter with Clean Architecture (Presentation, Application, Domain, Data)
- State Management: Riverpod
- Local DB: Drift (SQLite)
- Networking: Dio with Interceptors for JWT Refresh Tokens
- Rules: Always use const constructors. Keep build() methods lightweight. Extract UI components.
You are working on the UNZA Examination Attendance Flutter Application.

Project standards:

Architecture:
- Flutter Clean Architecture
- Feature-first folder structure
- Separation of presentation, domain, data layers

State Management:
- Riverpod only

Database:
- Drift ORM
- SQLite offline-first architecture

Networking:
- Dio
- JWT authentication
- Refresh token support
- Interceptors

Coding Rules:
- Prefer const constructors
- Keep build methods lightweight
- Never put business logic inside widgets
- Extract reusable widgets
- Avoid duplicated code
- Follow SOLID principles

UI Rules:
- Enterprise quality UI
- Consistent spacing system
- Responsive design
- Loading states required
- Error states required
- Empty states required
- Offline states required

Performance:
- Avoid unnecessary rebuilds
- Use ListView.builder
- Dispose controllers properly
- Use isolates for heavy computation

The application should feel like production software used by a university.